    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Nation?s first grid-connected energy storage installed and operationalized 
Indicator: 90% of at least 500 female high school students joining workshops and boot camps conducted across the country report increased understanding of career options and earning potential from careers in science, technology, engineering, and math and/or the energy sector 
Achievement: 0 
Progress/Status: The PowerUp bootcamp event at ITC was attended by 479 female students from Phnom Penh and the provinces. The Kirirom Food Production Facilities educational trip was attended by 33 female students. In total, 512 female students participated in person in both educational activities.
 
A post-event survey was conducted using Google Forms. It was shared with all schools and students, as well as on the Facebook page. The online survey evaluated the impact of the bootcamps on the participants and aimed to understand current barriers and gain insights on female students&amp;apos; choices regarding STEM/energy field studies. The survey results indicated that 100% of the female participants confirmed that participation in the event increased their interest and understanding of STEM and clean energy.
 
Data Source: Quarterly project progress reports</narrative>
